        <noteGrp type="abstract">
          <desc xml:lang="en">Abstract</desc>
          <note corresp="http://syriaca.org/nhsl" xml:lang="en" type="abstract" source="#bib5632-4 #bib5632-7">
            A hymn for the feast of the Epiphany, the second of fifteen attributed to <persName ref="http://syriaca.org/person/13">Ephrem</persName>. Structured as a year-by-year sequence through the thirty years of Christ's life, it calls on a different order of creation — Seraphim, angels, the heavens, the sun, the sea, the temple — to praise the Son in each successive year, opening with wordplay on the names Semha and Denha. The attribution is disputed.
          </note>
        </noteGrp>
        <noteGrp type="incipit">
          <desc xml:lang="en">Incipit</desc>
          <note xml:lang="la" type="incipit">
            <quote source="#bib5632-4">Imperante rege quem appellavere Semham Dominus noster ortus est in Judæa. Simul regnarunt Semha et Denha, rex in terra, Filius in cœlo. Cujus benedictum sit regnum!</quote>
          </note>
        </noteGrp>
